# TODO - Source-bound diff generator

## Objective

Implement `algorithms/diff/` as a generic deterministic generator that learns a
source-tree transformation from a local source/oracle pair and emits a
distributable transform whose target material remains bound to sufficiently
compatible source input.

The generic engine must remain agnostic to DOOM, C, Malbolge, and licensing
policy. Thin product recipes select paths, thresholds, domain probes, and output
format.

**Current implementation.**

- The public `DiffRecipe` now requires explicit `EXACT_BASELINE` or `COMPATIBLE`
  mode. `write_algorithm()` generates exact standalone Rust today; compatible
  mode
  remains fail-closed before output.
- Public recipe, identity, anchor, behavior, probe, provenance, payload,
  source-binding, exact/relocatable/compatible, and mapped/semantic metadata now
  validates exact runtime types before becoming evidence or touching output.
  Boolean numeric aliases, mutable collection substitutes, and foreign records
  fail through the owning domain boundary. Compatible mappers and postconditions
  also keep exceptions and foreign return records inside that boundary.
- The exact authoring planner/materializer reconstructs deterministic byte
  trees,
  reuses whole source files and source spans, and publishes only after full
  target
  verification.
- Synthetic tests cover exact reconstruction, deterministic planning, binary
  data,
  moves, modifications, creations, deletions, source mutation, and symlink
  failure.
- Generic identity helpers normalize line endings/optional whitespace, while the
  stable-anchor primitive uses rolling-content-selected sliding windows plus
  SHA-256
  fingerprints that survive offset shifts from insertions.
- Tree-level admission now separates symmetric structural similarity from
  asymmetric anchor survival, weights reference files equally, requires
  distributed
  matching files, and ignores candidate-only opaque size.
- Synthetic admission tests lock wrong-source rejection and the immediate
  representable thresholds above/below measured structural and anchor scores.
- Generic behavior evaluation now separates identity, compatibility, and bug
  semantics. Already-fixed bugs route corrections to skip; unavailable/unknown
  mandatory evidence fails closed.
- A conjunctive gate proves behavior-only clones cannot replace structural
  lineage
  and source lineage cannot replace failed compatibility behavior.
- Portable process probes now execute without shell interpolation, with
  structured
  roots, bounded time/output, isolated source mirrors, and deterministic
  selected-
  stdout transcripts.
- Behavior authoring derives identity transcripts from source and distinct bug
  `present`/`fixed` transcripts from source versus corrected oracle; a third
  candidate transcript becomes `unknown` and fails closed.
- The first DOOM executable identity probe compiles real candidate `m_fixed.c`
  against an MIT freestanding harness on an isolated mirror and digests its
  no-CRT
  PE exit code. Source and oracle matched in local calibration; synthetic
  fixtures
  provide repository-safe regression coverage.
- Source-binding calibration over the read-only DOOM source selected 127
  content-
  ranked distributed anchors. The modernized oracle recovered 105 shares against
  an
  84-share threshold at 0.66; the same experiment exposed and rejected an
  earlier
  offset-ranked sampler that recovered only 59.
- `src/research/algorithms/domain/algorithms/doom/generator/quality.py` records
  the first consumer recipe, and
  `doom.py` now supplies its C-aware Linux source identity view while excluding
  WAD
  and IPX surfaces from lineage scoring.
- The admission model combines structural similarity, stable anchors, and
  normalized
  behavior evidence. Threshold key unlock and authenticated exact-plan payload
  recovery are implemented; compatible in-memory placement now exists while
  protected
  compatible serialization/runtime emission remains unfinished.
- Source-binding recovery validates its entire threshold/share envelope before
  candidate inspection, including positive counts, canonical paths, exact digest
  and share lengths, and unique coordinates/source anchors; malformed metadata
  cannot lower the reconstruction threshold or be ignored as surplus evidence.
- The initial DOOM recipe records exploratory 0.50/0.66/0.80 thresholds.
  Synthetic
  threshold tests exist, and a local source-to-normalized-descendant stress
  smoke
  measured 0.780928 structural similarity and 0.766396 anchor coverage; broader
  source-variant and behavior calibration is still required before freezing
  them.
- Generic process-probe execution and behavior authoring are implemented. DOOM
  now
  has one executable fixed-point identity probe for Windows x86-64 / LLVM
  22.1.8;
  broader identity, compatibility, and bug coverage is still required.
- T-of-N GF(256) key splitting plus HKDF-SHA-256 anchor masking is implemented
  and
  covered by RFC/synthetic negative tests. Deterministic coefficient derivation
  is
  explicitly computational rather than information-theoretic and still requires
  independent cryptographic review.
- RFC 8439 ChaCha20-Poly1305 is implemented and locked to the official AEAD
  vector.
  Protected exact plans move all oracle literals into one authenticated
  ciphertext
  and bind its plan-specific key to distributed source anchors. The
  deterministic key
  schedule includes canonical source identity bytes that are not serialized into
  the
  transform, so transform metadata plus a guessed plaintext cannot derive the
  key by
  itself.
- A historical read-only DOOM smoke protected 2,116,232 literal bytes across 152
  instructions and materialized the then-current 152-file oracle snapshot. That
  snapshot is now known to include one accidental PowerShell root entry. The
  source-dependent key schedule rerun again matched exactly, left source/oracle
  snapshots unchanged, and its 4,655,420-byte generated Rust compiled to an
  object
  with Rust 1.97.1 and `-D warnings`.
- Exact protected plans emit as standalone std-only Rust. Authenticated
  passthrough
  roots are now excluded from static snapshots and copied from runtime input.
  With
  `data/` passthrough and the accidental oracle root excluded only in a
  temporary
  mirror, DOOM emitted 4,646,568 bytes of Rust and reproduced the intended
  151-file
  tree exactly under Rust GNU 1.97.1.
- Compatible/fuzzy Rust emission remains unfinished: consumer canonical
  identity,
  thresholds, behavior probes, and bug-routing still need runtime
  representation.

- Hash-only relocatable byte-range placement now preserves insertions inside
  stable
  source ranges and rejects missing/ambiguous boundaries before output. A
  synthetic
  boundary-change test deliberately still fails, defining the next mapped-token
  C
  placement milestone rather than pretending byte relocation solves
  reformatting.

- Generic mapped semantic placement now hashes canonical units, uniquely locates
  them
  in candidate source, maps them back to raw spans, preserves unrelated raw
  bytes, and
  re-tokenizes post-edit output to reject unsafe seams.
- The DOOM C mapper is identity-equivalent to the established canonicalizer
  across a
  read-only 273-file / 549,978-unit source+oracle smoke with zero mismatches.
  Synthetic
  placement preserves comments, formatting, and unrelated upstream functions.

- Compatible tree authoring now composes lineage + behavior admission, semantic
  placement, conservative opaque exact gates, target-only conflict checks,
  candidate-
  only preservation, historical removals, and transactional postconditions. Bug
  correction routes still fail closed until correction IDs are attached to
  edits.
- Replacing generic sequence matching with unique 8/4/2/1-unit k-gram anchors +
  LIS
  reduced the full read-only DOOM compatible-plan smoke from runner timeout to
  11.159
  seconds. The plan contains 117 semantic-patch files / 6,257 edits / 251,933
  raw
  replacement bytes, 7 candidate copies, 2 exact-gated opaque files, and 26
  creates.

- Exact external source revision pins are now generic infrastructure. The DOOM
  quality
  domain hard-pins `id-Software/DOOM@a77dfb96cb91780ca334d0d4cfd86957558007e0`
  and verifies 165 official files against deterministic snapshot SHA-256
  `20f6b67369b98c3f62b7c8ff34493ef9647c88bce7b85c82b9ecd72bad336d8b`; `data/`
  remains outside that code pin.

- `passthrough_roots` are authenticated plan metadata. Source/oracle must match
  there
  during authoring, but later runtime bytes and candidate-only files under those
  roots
  are preserved without changing the exact static source identity.
- Exact snapshots, passthrough copies, revision-pin roots, and the DOOM C/H
  lineage view now use error-reporting recursive walks; inaccessible subtrees
  fail closed instead of disappearing from source identity or provenance.

## Acceptance

- Exact baseline source plus emitted transform reproduces the local oracle
  byte-for-byte.
- Comments and formatting may be ignored for source identity without being
  silently discarded from preserved output/provenance.
- Content/token anchors tolerate non-semantic insertions better than absolute
  byte
  offsets.
- Identity, compatibility, and bug probes have separate semantics.
- An upstream source that already satisfies a bug-fix postcondition can remain
  compatible without reproducing the original bug.
- Generated transform without enough admitted source cannot materialize the
  target.
- Unrelated source and behavior-only clones fail closed.
- Source-binding failure occurs before accepted target files are published.
- Generic tests contain no third-party DOOM source.
- Generation and exact-baseline materialization are deterministic and
  byte-identical across repeated runs.
- Threshold values are justified by calibration evidence and documented as
  technical policy rather than legal conclusions.
- Jig repository validation passes without weakening project governance.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `algorithms/diff/`,
  `docs/technical/tooling/source-bound-diff-generator.md`, and synthetic tests.
- First integration consumer:
  `src/research/algorithms/domain/algorithms/doom/generator/quality.py`.
- Second integration consumer:
  `src/research/algorithms/domain/algorithms/doom/generator/amalgamate.py`,
